  tasks / checklists   117 tasks all checked; checklists 120/120

Audited against project-instructions.md v1.2.8. Principles I, II, III, V and VII
each re-checked against the live payload and the contract.

The release gate is closed by amendment, not by exception. E010's plan declared
that the feature could not pass QC while specs/sad.md, the plan's summary table
and contracts/openapi.yaml named three addresses. Governance places amendments to
registered documents on the default branch, so the branch recorded the need and
did not act on it. The amendment landed on main as 24456b9 and is merged here;
four sites now resolve to GET /api/v1/worklist without the reader composing
anything. QC iterations 1-3 never checked the condition; iteration 4 found it.

Not release-blocking, and carried forward rather than closed here:
  - SC-017 and SC-018 are measured against 16 lines rather than the working
    population. Recorded in plan.md:186 in Principle VII's four-part form, with
    the note that E005's set is not the answer — it holds 199 lines of which only
    24 are open.
  - pip-audit has produced no result on either side and is recorded as
    unmeasured rather than as a null result.
  - The security limitation's reversal trigger has fired for /src/web: 3 high
    advisories on production dependencies. E001 scaffold work.

Per-iteration findings, severities and measurements are in qc-report.md, one
section per iteration.
